    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Paris graphic design studio founded 2008 by Romain Rachlin and Maxime Tetard (both ENSAD alumni), later joined by Cyril Taieb and Francois Dubois. Studio has publicly stated it intends to remain small; core team of ~4 with freelancers. Practice spans graphic design, custom type design (10+ named typefaces including Alsace, Berline, Lorraine), photography, art direction, and identity systems. Clients include Hermes, Bourse de Commerce Pinault Collection, Centre Pompidou-Metz, Louvre Abu Dhabi, Christian Dior, and Diptyque. Won European Design Agency of the Year 2011. Senior creative-director level founders; Autonomy 5 (self-directed studio, sets its own creative direction). LinkedIn lists 13 employees but studio self-description and multiple sources consistently describe a small team of ~4 core members; 2-10 size retained. Sources: les-graphiquants.fr/en, Wikipedia, LinkedIn company page.",
